														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3096330">
									

<p>Maybe it's just me: I'm lazy, depressed and have a lot of things to read during the day.</p>
<p>When I see a crosslink to an article, and I can just open it up, read the first line of the description, go, &quot;Oh yeah, I remember that&quot; and be on the same page as the article it was linked from, it's fine. When I have to reread the entire article, or worse, a series of tales, to make sure I have every detail so I know how they relate to the new article, I'm just gonna close the whole thing down and read nothing. I come here expecting articles I can read and enjoy in a few minutes. Maybe I'm in the minority.</p>

							</div>

								
					
